Q22. What is a FactoryBean? <p>Answer: A <code>FactoryBean&lt;T&gt;</code> is a Spring bean whose <code>getObject()</code> produces another bean. Used for complex bean creation (e.g., <code>SqlSessionFactoryBean</code>, <code>LocalContainerEntityManagerFactoryBean</code>). Retrieved by prefixing <code>&amp;</code> to get the factory itself.</p> <pre><code>public class MyFactoryBean implements FactoryBean&lt;MyBean&gt; {
    public MyBean getObject() { return new MyBean(); }
    public Class&lt;?&gt; getObjectType() { return MyBean.class; }
    public boolean isSingleton() { return true; }
}
</code></pre>

