);
</code></pre>

Programmatic (Sink / Processor) <pre><code>Sinks.Many&lt;String&gt; sink = Sinks.many().multicast().onBackpressureBuffer();
Flux&lt;String&gt; flux = sink.asFlux();
sink.tryEmitNext("Hello");
sink.tryEmitComplete();

// Replay
Sinks.Many&lt;String&gt; replay = Sinks.many().replay().all();

// Unicast (single subscriber)
Sinks.Many&lt;String&gt; unicast = Sinks.many().unicast().onBackpressureBuffer();
</code></pre> <p>Older API: <code>FluxProcessor</code>, <code>UnicastProcessor</code>, <code>EmitterProcessor</code> — replaced by <code>Sinks</code> in Reactor 3.4+.</p>

Hot vs Cold <ul> <li>Cold — each subscriber triggers a fresh start (<code>Flux.range</code>, <code>Mono.just</code>)</li> <li>Hot — emits regardless of subscribers (<code>ConnectableFlux</code>, <code>Sinks</code>)</li> </ul> <pre><code>ConnectableFlux&lt;Long&gt; hot = Flux.interval(Duration.ofSeconds(1)).publish();
hot.connect();   // starts emitting
hot.subscribe(System.out::println);
Thread.sleep(5000);
hot.subscribe(System.out::println);   // misses earlier emissions
</code></pre>

